Description: Keep real-time cadence checks out of shared Launchpad builds
 The three real-timer cadence tests impose millisecond tolerances that shared
 builders cannot guarantee. Keep deterministic pacing, stall arithmetic,
 stop/resume, simulation, allocation and parity coverage enabled in Debian.
 These cadence tests remain enabled in the unpatched upstream/CI source.
Author: Matthew Stanton <stantonmatthewj@gmail.com>
Origin: upstream
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-02
--- a/tests/test_presentationclock.cpp
+++ b/tests/test_presentationclock.cpp
@@ -243,6 +243,8 @@
 
     void clockUsesFixedPhase()
     {
+        QSKIP("Wall-clock cadence is validated in upstream CI");
+
         QFETCH(int, target);
         QFETCH(int, submissionDelayMs);
         QQuickWindow window; // No real rendering; supply synthetic swap feedback.
@@ -325,6 +327,8 @@
 
     void synchronousWorkDoesNotExtendTimerPeriod()
     {
+        QSKIP("Wall-clock cadence is validated in upstream CI");
+
         // An unexposed window has no scene-graph swaps, exercising the actual
         // fallback timer rather than just the scheduling calculation.
         QQuickWindow window;
@@ -387,6 +391,8 @@
 
     void renderedFeedbackIncludesStallTime()
     {
+        QSKIP("Wall-clock cadence is validated in upstream CI");
+
